# Build context for Dockerfile.fleet is the repo root, but the image only COPYs
# lab/skeleton, lab/tests, lab/pytest.ini. Exclude everything heavy or secret so
# `gcloud builds submit .` uploads a small, secret-free context.

# Dependencies / build artifacts
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/build
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/*.pyc
**/.venv
**/venv

# VCS / tooling
.git
.gitignore
.claude
.harness

# Secrets / local env — NEVER ship into a build context
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.vercel
**/*-secret
**/.worker-secret

# Not needed by the fleet image
web
docs
scripts
*.md
# control-plane is deliberately NOT excluded wholesale: Dockerfile.eve-fleet COPYs
# control-plane/drainer. The only heavy part (control-plane/node_modules, 91M) is
# already dropped by **/node_modules above, and control-plane/.env.local by **/.env.*
# — so the drainer ships without needing a broad exclusion + `!` re-include (whose
# subdir-of-excluded-dir semantics differ across docker builders). control-plane/convex
# (~256K, unused by the image) just rides along in the context, harmlessly.
